;; ---
;; --- Install the user-facing scripts of this directory.
;; ---
;; Until now nothing installed them, and the documentation -- written for people who do NOT
;; have the sources -- called them by their bare names all the same. Marionnet itself now
;; NAMES one of them on screen (bin/marionnet.ml, the startup warning about the run
;; directories left behind) and RUNS it from a button, which settles the question: the tool
;; a program tells the user to run has to exist on the user's PATH.
;;
;; They go into the scripts/ subdirectory of the share section, i.e. where the scripts of
;; bin/dune and bashbricks.sh land -- for an ordinary install
;;   /usr/local/share/marionnet/scripts/
;; -- because the Makefile mirrors ALL of share/marionnet/scripts/* into $(PREFIX)/bin/ (hard
;; links for `install-final-as-root', symlinks for `install-for-testing'), making them
;; executable on the way. That mirror is the whole point here, and it is why nothing has to
;; be added to the Makefile.
;;
;; mrnctl and mrn2sh are SYMLINKS in the source tree; dune installs them as copies, which
;; changes nothing: both scripts choose their behaviour from `${0##*/}' (see PROGNAME in
;; marionnet-ctl and mrn-check), never from the inode they were reached through.
;;
;; Deliberately not installed: marionnet_from_scratch (a dead installer, see
;; docs/modernisation-installation-marionnet.md), its two satellites and
;; make_marionnet_bytecode_revno (a development-time tool). Note that the whole directory is
;; covered by a `useful-scripts/*' line of .gitignore: what git tracks here is the short list
;; of files someone chose to track, not what the directory happens to contain. The bash
;; completion
;; (marionnet-completion.bash) is not a command and belongs to a completion directory, not
;; to bin/: it is written down as a remaining task of the installation work-stream.
;; ---
(install
  (files
     ;; --- The clients of the control channel (work-stream `pilotage-par-script'), which the
     ;; --- delivered documentation (doc-src/scripting/) calls by their bare names. The two
     ;; --- links are part of the interface: they select the behaviour by $0.
     (marionnet-ctl as scripts/marionnet-ctl)
     (mrnctl as scripts/mrnctl)
     (mrn-check as scripts/mrn-check)
     (mrn2sh as scripts/mrn2sh))
  (section share)
  (package marionnet))
